{"school":{"dbn":"11X529","name":"One World Middle School at Edenwald","boro":"Bronx","district":"11","district_label":"District 11","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":310,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"3750 BAYCHESTER AVENUE, BRONX, NY 10466","phone":"718-547-1890","website":"www.owms.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/63379","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"One World Middle School is a small school committed to understanding 'who' the child is in order to teach them. Our school is modeled after the United Nations and when children enter, they are referred to as Ambassadors-in-Training until they become ambassadors. Our multifaceted curriculum includes High School Regents courses, Civic Engagement, Music, Orchestra, Band, STEM, Farming, Art, and Coding. We believe a well-rounded education is the key to success. We see Broadway shows, take part in Acts of Kindness and ensure our ambassadors have opportunities to travel overnight. We have visited Historically Black Colleges, Harvard, Yale, Northeastern, SUNY schools, Georgetown to name a few. We have explored the Rocky Mountains to Niagara Falls. In the past 5 years, ambassadors have walked the path of great Civil Rights activists by visiting places such as Selma, Martin Luther King's childhood home, Little Rock Nine and the Lorraine Hotel. We are proud to be an ASD NEST where our staff is dedicated to understanding the needs of all children and developing relationships to ensure success. Teachers will stay late, proctor study hall or bring children up for lunch to help them. Highlights include Orchestra, Basketball, Track, Flag Football, Broadway Jr., Dancing, Art, Spoken Word.  We have partnerships with Google, Education through Music, DREAM and Mouse. We also earned the honor of being named a Respect for All School for the past 4 years.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","